**Why should you join our team?**

Innergex Renewable Energy Inc. is an independent renewable energy producer with an extensive and growing portfolio of assets in Canada, the United States, France and Chile. The Corporation develops, acquires, owns and operates hydroelectric facilities, wind farms, solar farms and energy storage facilities.

For more than 30 years, Innergex has believed in a world where abundant renewable energy promotes healthier communities and creates shared prosperity. We are convinced that generating power from renewable sources will lead the way to a better world. We remain committed to responsible growth that balances people, our planet, and prosperity. We believe in offering an engaging, inclusive and supportive work environment where each team member can thrive.

**Your contribution!**

Reporting to the Senior Manager - IT Infrastructure, the Systems Administrator plays a key role in the operation, evolution, and security of the company’s technology environments. Working alongside a team of specialists, the person ensures the smooth operation of hybrid infrastructures (on-premises and cloud-based) that support Innergex’s corporate operations and renewable energy facilities in Canada, the United States, France, and Chile. They participate in large-scale technology projects, the optimization of IT and OT environments, process automation, and the maintenance of high standards of performance, availability, and cybersecurity. The person in this role will be required to participate in a rotating on-call schedule to ensure support for critical infrastructure outside of normal working hours, including evenings and weekends.

**Your day-to day!**

* Administer and evolve Windows, Azure, Microsoft 365, and VMware environments.
* Ensure the operation of hybrid infrastructures (on-premises and cloud-based) and data centers.
* Manage essential services such as Active Directory, Entra ID, Exchange, VDI, virtual servers, and SaaS/PaaS solutions.
* Analyze system performance, capacity, and security to ensure stability and availability.
* Participate in the implementation of new technological solutions and the continuous improvement of infrastructure.
* Help resolve complex incidents and serve as a technical expert for internal teams.
* Monitor IT environments and respond to security and operational alerts.
* Collaborate with operations and construction teams to support renewable energy production sites.
* Automate certain administrative tasks using scripts and appropriate tools.
* Participate in system updates, scheduled maintenance, and optimization.
* Participate in a rotating on-call schedule and contribute to operational continuity by providing support for critical infrastructure when required.
* Maintain thorough and up-to-date technical documentation.
* Contribute to audits, IT controls, and adherence to compliance and cybersecurity requirements.
* Serve as an advisor to the team on best practices and emerging technologies.

**Your skills, our requirements!**

* Bilingualism (French and English, both spoken and written) is required to collaborate with various stakeholders outside Quebec on a regular basis.
* A minimum of 3 years of experience in systems administration
* Must be available and able to participate in a rotating on-call schedule and contribute to business continuity by providing support for critical infrastructure when required.

**Additional considerations!**

* The position is based at the company’s headquarters in Longueuil, steps away from the Longueuil-Université de Sherbrooke metro station.
* This position is at the P2 level.
* Competitive salary and annual bonus;
* Three weeks vacation to start and paid vacations during the holiday season;
* 100% Innergex-funded medical insurance from day one of employment, including primary care services through dialogue (or telemedicine) for permanent positions;
* Group retirement plans with employer participation;
* 100% Employer-funded Wellness Account;
* Electric vehicle (E-VIP) incentive program;
* Hybrid work model;
* Career development opportunities;
* Offices accessible by public transportation.

**Our benefits!**

* Competitive salary and annual bonus;
* Three weeks vacation to start and paid vacations during the holiday season;
* 100% Innergex-funded medical insurance from day one of employment, including primary care services through dialogue (or telemedicine) for permanent positions;
* Group retirement plans with employer participation;
* 100% Employer-funded Wellness Account;
* Electric vehicle (E-VIP) incentive program;
* Hybrid work model;
* Career development opportunities;
* Offices accessible by public transportation.

Innergex is an equal opportunity employer that values each person’s unique background, diversity, experiences, perspectives and talents. Innergex is committed to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment and bases all employment decisions on business needs, job requirements and individual qualifications. The key to our success as a global company is to recruit, develop and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.

**www.innergex.com**

Please note that only selected candidates will be contacted.

